    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nFirst of all, big thanks for all your work and the great plugins. I'm a big fan! :heart: \r\n\r\nI use my own nvim config with the help of lazy.nvim as plugin manager.\r\n\r\nActually, everything works perfectly, only 3-4 LSP keymaps for Mini.Pick are not \"working\".\r\n\r\n\r\nNo matter in which project and language, when I use one of the following keybindings I always get a \"_E79 cannot expand wildcards_\" error message\r\n\r\ne.g.:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>ci\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='implementation'<CR>\", { desc = \"Implementations\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cR\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='references'<CR>\", { desc = \"References\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cs\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='document_symbol'<CR>\", { desc = \"Symbols buffer\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnly after pressing a button the pick window pops up with the correct result.\r\n\r\nIs this normal or am I missing something?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`settings.lua`\r\n\r\n_E79 cannot expand wildcards:_\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>ci\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='implementation'<CR>\", { desc = \"Implementations\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cR\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='references'<CR>\", { desc = \"References\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cs\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='document_symbol'<CR>\", { desc = \"Symbols buffer\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cS\", \"<cmd>Pick lsp scope='workspace_symbol'<CR>\", { desc = \"Symbols workspace\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this one there is no error message and the pick window appears directly:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cd\", \"<cmd>Pick diagnostic scope='current'<CR>\", { desc = \"Diagnostic buffer\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>cD\", \"<cmd>Pick diagnostic scope='all'<CR>\", { desc = \"Diagnostic workspace\" })\r\n```\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThat the pick window appears directly without pressing any keys.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/49953458/17b78d53-4140-4de1-9f88-0cfa21ea520a)\r\n",
